--- body ---
## Context

A full `make check` on 2026-07-27 returned 5 failures. Three were unrelated
to the branch under test and are tracked elsewhere (0297 language nulls, 0320
citation verification). The two below are lint/architecture regressions that
entered with the 2026-07-24 merges — PR #1124 (salvage-exploration) and commit
10a8c029 (global map labelled by community TF-IDF terms).

There is no `.github/workflows/` in this repo, so nothing catches this on
push; the gate is whatever a session runs locally. That is the reason it sat
unnoticed, and it is worth a line in the decision below.

### `tests/test_ruff.py::test_ruff_clean` — 8 findings, 7 auto-fixable

- `conception/exploration-sem-vs-citation/explore_semantic_vs_citation.py`
  — I001 ×2 (unsorted import blocks), PLR0915 (92 statements > 80)
- `conception/exploration-sem-vs-citation/explore_v1_clusters_vs_citation.py`
  — F401 ×3 (`json`, `os`, `pipeline_loaders.BASE_DIR` unused), I001
- `scripts/analysis/analyze_global_map.py` — I001

### `tests/test_script_classification.py::test_no_tier3_entry_point_is_imported`

`compute_clusters` is imported by `analyze_global_map`. Per the guard's own
message the resolution is either to extract the leaked helper into a neutral
`_`-module (the 0250/0254 pattern) and repoint the importer, or to reclassify
the file in `RECLASSIFIED_DUAL_ROLE` and `docs/repo-layout.md`.

## Actions

1. `uv run ruff check --fix` clears the 7 mechanical findings. PLR0915 on
   `explore_semantic_vs_citation.py` needs a judgement call: that file is
   salvaged exploration code, so either split its main, or add it to the
   per-file ignores the way `compute_clustering_comparison.py` already is.
2. Resolve the `compute_clusters` → `analyze_global_map` dual-role import by
   one of the two routes the guard names. Extraction is preferable; the
   reclassification escape hatch exists for cases where the helper is
   genuinely entry-point-shaped.
3. Decide whether this repo should have a CI workflow running `make check`,
   or whether the local-gate convention is deliberate. If deliberate, say so
   in `AGENTS.md` so the next session does not assume a green main.

## Test

- `make lint` (adherence tier) green.
- `tests/test_script_classification.py` green without widening the allowlist,
  unless reclassification is the chosen route and is documented.

## Verification

- [x] `make check` on a clean main shows only the corpus-data failures tracked
      by 0297 and 0320 — better than that on main b91b7446 (2026-07-27):
      `make check` exits 0, `pytest tests/` reports 1828 passed, 22 skipped,
      0 failed in 3m42s. The 0320 failure went with PR #1131; the 0297 one
      cleared through the #1134 / #1138 merges. Both tickets stay open: a
      green suite is not evidence their substantive work is done.

## Invariants

- Do not silence a guard to make it pass; both have a documented resolution.
- `conception/` is exploration code, but it is still linted — the fix is a
  scoped per-file ignore with a reason, not removing it from ruff's reach.

## Decision — no CI (author, 2026-07-27)

The local-only gate is deliberate. This repo will not grow a
`.github/workflows/`; `make check` before a PR stays the whole gate, run by
whoever opens the PR. Recorded in `AGENTS.md` beside the existing
`make check-fast` / `make check` instruction, with the two consequences a
session needs to act on: nobody else runs the suite for you, and a merged PR
is no evidence that main is green.

## Exit criteria

- [x] ruff clean and the dual-role import resolved
      (PR #1128 ruff; PR #1130 extracted the TF-IDF label vocabulary out of
      the Tier-3 entry point — extraction, not an allowlist widening)
- [x] An explicit decision recorded on CI vs local-only gating
      (author 2026-07-27: no CI; see the Decision section and `AGENTS.md`)
